WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-US

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:00.810
Here's the truth.

00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:06.300
I work with people all the time who

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:08.490
tell me incredible things and then

00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:10.470
say, do you really think anyone

00:00:10.470 --> 00:00:12.630
wants to hear what I have to say?

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:13.800
And when people say that

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:15.660
to me, I tell them this.

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:18.420
I spend a week at a yoga retreat

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:20.070
center teaching storytelling

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:20.845
to about a dozen people.

00:00:21.630 --> 00:00:22.830
The deal I have with them is

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:24.540
this, you never have to speak.

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:26.220
If you don't want to come in like

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:27.930
a mushroom, sit down and learn.

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:30.119
No one ever does that except for

00:00:30.119 --> 00:00:32.759
once someone did a woman, she

00:00:32.759 --> 00:00:35.310
actually sat right next to me all

00:00:35.310 --> 00:00:37.140
week long and never said a word.

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:40.379
On the last day of our class, a Sunday

00:00:40.379 --> 00:00:42.239
morning, people are going around

00:00:42.239 --> 00:00:44.580
and sharing stories, and my mushroom

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:46.890
to my right finally makes a sound.

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:48.180
She says, well.

00:00:49.214 --> 00:00:51.525
I have something, I just don't know

00:00:51.525 --> 00:00:52.995
if anyone would want to hear it.

00:00:53.565 --> 00:00:54.434
And I said, well, tell it

00:00:54.434 --> 00:00:55.964
to us and we will decide.

00:00:56.265 --> 00:00:58.095
So this is the story she tells us.

00:00:58.214 --> 00:01:00.675
She said she was doing yoga one night

00:01:01.004 --> 00:01:03.194
till about seven o'clock, and then she

00:01:03.194 --> 00:01:04.905
got in her car and for the first time

00:01:04.905 --> 00:01:06.585
in a long time, she had felt peace.

00:01:06.795 --> 00:01:08.985
She had finally sort of let go of the

00:01:08.985 --> 00:01:11.625
anger and resentment inside her and she

00:01:11.625 --> 00:01:13.545
was feeling good as she was driving home.

00:01:14.324 --> 00:01:15.854
And then this car came

00:01:15.854 --> 00:01:17.025
barreling up behind her.

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:19.890
Her like tailgating, her weaving all

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:21.930
over the road, and then all of that

00:01:21.930 --> 00:01:24.750
time she spent finding centeredness

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:26.910
and peace in that yoga class.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:28.200
It was gone instantly.

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:29.790
She was angry at the person behind

00:01:29.790 --> 00:01:32.100
her, and then that person flew around

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:35.070
her, went ahead and hit a pole,

00:01:35.670 --> 00:01:37.590
wrapped the car around a telephone

00:01:37.590 --> 00:01:40.170
pole, so she pulled over, she got out

00:01:40.170 --> 00:01:41.670
of the car and she ran over and she

00:01:41.670 --> 00:01:43.110
found the driver behind the wheel.

00:01:43.350 --> 00:01:44.580
Very badly injured.

00:01:44.910 --> 00:01:46.200
So she called 9 1 1.

00:01:46.410 --> 00:01:47.940
Now she was up in the Berkshires

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:49.170
in Massachusetts, sort of

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:50.190
in the middle of nowhere.

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:52.470
And so the 9 1 1 operator said,

00:01:52.710 --> 00:01:54.240
I need you to begin administering

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:55.920
first aid 'cause the ambulance is

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:57.300
gonna take a while to get there.

00:01:57.630 --> 00:01:59.580
So listening to the 9 1 1

00:01:59.580 --> 00:02:01.050
operator, she began working

00:02:01.050 --> 00:02:03.030
on this man behind the wheel.

00:02:03.660 --> 00:02:05.670
Eventually the ambulance arrives and

00:02:05.670 --> 00:02:07.680
they take over, but the ambulance

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:09.329
driver says, I need you to follow

00:02:09.329 --> 00:02:10.979
me to the hospital because you were

00:02:10.979 --> 00:02:12.329
with him for the first 10 minutes.

00:02:12.329 --> 00:02:13.590
The doctors might wanna talk to you.

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:15.570
She's annoyed about the whole

00:02:15.570 --> 00:02:17.190
thing, but she agrees to go.

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:18.990
So she follows the ambulance at the

00:02:18.990 --> 00:02:21.030
hospital and she takes her place in the

00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:22.650
waiting room to see if the doctors need

00:02:22.650 --> 00:02:25.050
to talk to her while she's waiting.

00:02:25.110 --> 00:02:26.910
In the waiting room, a woman

00:02:26.910 --> 00:02:29.820
walks in, her best friend, she

00:02:29.820 --> 00:02:31.440
says, what are you doing here?

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:33.450
And her best friend says, my

00:02:33.450 --> 00:02:35.520
husband was just in a car accident.

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:38.100
He put his car into a telephone pole.

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:40.500
The woman had never met her

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:41.910
best friend's husband before.

00:02:42.329 --> 00:02:43.950
They had never encountered each other

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:46.079
because the husband worked the night shift

00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:48.030
and so they had never seen each other.

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:50.190
The husband dies.

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:55.020
That man who she treated died shortly

00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:57.270
thereafter, and her best friend

00:02:57.270 --> 00:02:59.460
says to her, I'm so glad that in

00:02:59.460 --> 00:03:01.200
my husband's final moments on this

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:03.600
earth, he was with someone I loved.

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:07.110
She tells us that story in that

00:03:07.110 --> 00:03:09.030
workshop, my mushroom, who doesn't

00:03:09.030 --> 00:03:11.519
speak all week, and then she says to us.

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:13.380
Do you really think that's a

00:03:13.380 --> 00:03:15.210
story anyone would want to hear?

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:18.750
At that point, we're all crying and

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:23.220
I can't imagine what it takes or

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:24.930
what might have happened to this

00:03:24.930 --> 00:03:27.420
woman to think that that story

00:03:27.870 --> 00:03:29.790
doesn't want to be heard by everyone.

00:03:30.330 --> 00:03:31.410
And yet, here's the truth.

00:03:32.070 --> 00:03:34.530
I work with people all the time who

00:03:34.530 --> 00:03:36.690
tell me incredible things and then

00:03:36.690 --> 00:03:38.640
say, do you really think anyone

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:41.010
wants to hear what I have to say?

00:03:41.730 --> 00:03:43.380
And what I always tell people is this,

00:03:44.459 --> 00:03:46.920
if it means something to you, it will

00:03:46.920 --> 00:03:48.690
mean something to other people too.

00:03:49.410 --> 00:03:51.209
I think the tragedy of this world

00:03:51.209 --> 00:03:52.590
is that many of us walk through the

00:03:52.590 --> 00:03:54.810
world thinking that the moments of our

00:03:54.810 --> 00:03:58.170
lives are meaningful only to us when

00:03:58.170 --> 00:04:00.090
the world needs to hear your stories.

00:04:00.450 --> 00:04:02.160
The world needed to hear that woman's

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:04.709
story, and yet she sat there for a week

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:06.930
wondering if anyone wanted to hear it.

00:04:07.109 --> 00:04:08.670
I don't want that to be the case for you.

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:09.870
If you have something in

00:04:09.870 --> 00:04:10.829
your heart and your mind.

00:04:11.205 --> 00:04:13.155
That means something to you that touches

00:04:13.155 --> 00:04:14.955
your heart and mind in a meaningful way.

00:04:15.225 --> 00:04:16.695
I promise you other people

00:04:16.695 --> 00:04:17.385
want to hear it too.

00:04:17.985 --> 00:04:19.065
They'll even wanna hear

00:04:19.065 --> 00:04:20.355
it if you tell it poorly.

00:04:21.435 --> 00:04:24.255
The right story told poorly is

00:04:24.255 --> 00:04:25.845
still a great story to tell.

00:04:26.445 --> 00:04:28.605
So ask yourself, does

00:04:28.605 --> 00:04:29.565
it mean something to me?

00:04:31.065 --> 00:04:33.105
And if it does, I promise you it

00:04:33.105 --> 00:04:34.935
will mean something to others too.

